envelope "Attleboro documented Remote or Hand authority choice"

Guideline
    This is a research procedure-choice envelope, not plant service proof.
    Angel chooses one of two documented command locations when eligible.
    The normal Remote branch needs utility, utility MTS, no generator run,
    Remote selector, cleared Power Fail Reset latch, and no trip.
    The generator Hand branch needs generator MTS, generator readiness,
    local Hand selector, local operator, and no trip.
    The game proves command-location eligibility only. Physical delivery,
    run feedback, flow and observation are separate obligations.

Definitions
    Definitions
    End.

    ProgramVariables
        Real utility; Real mtsGen; Real genRun; Real genReady;
        Real selectorRemote; Real selectorHand; Real localActor;
        Real trip; Real resetPending; Real startDemand;
        Real remoteCmd; Real handCmd;
    End.

precondition
    startDemand = 1
    & (
      (utility = 1 & mtsGen = 0 & genRun = 0
       & selectorRemote = 1 & resetPending = 0 & trip = 0)
      |
      (mtsGen = 1 & genReady = 1 & selectorHand = 1
       & localActor = 1 & trip = 0)
    )

postcondition
    (remoteCmd = 1 & handCmd = 0
     & utility = 1 & mtsGen = 0 & genRun = 0
     & selectorRemote = 1 & resetPending = 0 & trip = 0)
    |
    (remoteCmd = 0 & handCmd = 1
     & mtsGen = 1 & genReady = 1 & selectorHand = 1
     & localActor = 1 & trip = 0)

game
    {
        {
            ? (utility = 1 & mtsGen = 0 & genRun = 0
               & selectorRemote = 1 & resetPending = 0 & trip = 0);
            remoteCmd := 1;
            handCmd := 0;
        }
        ++
        {
            ? (mtsGen = 1 & genReady = 1 & selectorHand = 1
               & localActor = 1 & trip = 0);
            remoteCmd := 0;
            handCmd := 1;
        }
    }
